hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15480","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Zakariya, from al-Shabi, from al-Harith ibn Malik Ibn Barsa, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of the conquest of Makkah saying: This, meaning, will not be raided after today until the Day of Resurrection."
"15481","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Zakariya narrated to me, from Amir, he said: Al-Harith ibn Malik Ibn Barsa said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying on the day of the conquest of Makkah, and he said: It will not be raided after it until the Day of Resurrection."
